        <headline>Severe Thunderstorm Warning issued September 25 at 3:43PM MDT until September 25 at 4:30PM MDT by NWS Albuquerque NM</headline>
        <description>SVRABQ

The National Weather Service in Albuquerque has issued a

* Severe Thunderstorm Warning for...
South Central Mora County in northeastern New Mexico...
Northwestern San Miguel County in northeastern New Mexico...

* Until 430 PM MDT.

* At 343 PM MDT, a severe thunderstorm was located over Las Vegas,
moving northeast at 30 mph.

HAZARD...60 mph wind gusts and quarter size hail.

SOURCE...Radar indicated.

IMPACT...Hail damage to vehicles is expected. Expect wind damage to
roofs, siding, and trees.

* Locations impacted include...
Las Vegas, Storrie Lake State Park, Montezuma, Sapello,
Romeroville, Watrous, Tecolote, Golondrinas and Ojitos Frios.

This includes the following highways...
State Road 518 between Mile Markers 1 and 13. Interstate 25 between
Mile Markers 336 and 365...and near Mile Marker 366. State Road 104
between Mile Markers 1 and 11.
</description>
        <instruction>Seek shelter inside a well-built structure and stay away from
windows. This storm is capable of producing damaging winds and large
hail.

Motorists can expect brief but sudden changes in visibility and
ponding of water on roadways as storms move through the area.</instruction>
